Okay, let's evaluate the 'Mercedes-Benz CLS CLS320 CDI'.

Similar to the 'CLS 250 CDI', the "CLS 320 CDI" designation belongs to an older generation of the CLS, specifically the first generation (Type C219, approx. 2004-2010). This model used a 3.0L V6 turbo-diesel engine.

You've asked for the *most recent version* related to this nameplate. In the current CLS generation (Type C257, 2018-present), the role of the higher-performance, six-cylinder diesel is filled by the **Mercedes-Benz CLS 400d**. This model uses a modern 3.0L inline-six turbo-diesel engine with 4MATIC all-wheel drive.

Therefore, I will evaluate the **Mercedes-Benz CLS 400d (C257)** as the most relevant modern counterpart to the older CLS 320 CDI.

